From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Mon, 07 Sep 2026 20:49:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: add linear active cooling governor with passive
 step-wise control

Local implementation against Linux 6.12.103; not an upstream backport.
Interpolate each active cooling map within its limits up to the next
higher active trip bound to that device in the same zone. Keep core
hysteresis, maximum-demand aggregation, and hot/critical handling. Reuse
step-wise trip updates for passive cooling so a zone can manage both
fans and CPU throttling. Allow selecting linear as the built-in default,
with no userspace selector or new thermal DT properties. Document the
policy and exercise it through the real thermal core using simulated
sensors and cooling devices.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
